# RemoteOps — IE3090 Network Programming (Part 1)

**Registration number:** @@REGNO@@

| Item | Calculation | Value |
|---|---|---|
| Agent listening port | 7000 + first four digits of numeric part (@@NUM@@ → @@FIRST4@@) | **@@PORT@@** |
| Source files | last three digits = @@L3@@ | `agent_@@L3@@.c`, `controller_@@L3@@.c`, `Makefile_@@L3@@` |
| Session ID tag | last four digits (@@LAST4@@) reversed | **SID:@@SID@@** |
| Auth token | `OPS-` + last four digits | **@@TOKEN@@** |
| Log file | `remoteops_<regno>.log` | `@@LOGFILE@@` |
| Storage path | `./agentfiles/<regno>/<filename>` | `./agentfiles/@@REGNO@@/` |
| Archive | `IE3090_<regno>.zip` | `IE3090_@@REGNO@@.zip` |

## Build
```
make -f Makefile_@@L3@@
```
Requires gcc and pthreads on Linux. No external libraries.

## Run
```
./agent_@@L3@@                       # terminal 1 (server / managed machine)
./controller_@@L3@@ 127.0.0.1 @@PORT@@     # terminal 2 (client); auto-sends AUTH @@TOKEN@@
./controller_@@L3@@ 127.0.0.1 @@PORT@@ noauth   # to test authentication manually
```
Controller commands: `SYSINFO`, `LISTPROC`, `EXEC <DATE|UPTIME|DISKFREE|HOSTNAME|WHOAMI>`,
`PUT <localpath> [remotename]`, `GET <remotename> [localpath]`, `MONITOR START <udpport>`, `MONITOR STOP`, `QUIT`.

## Test
`./test.sh` builds, starts an Agent, and runs the full test suite (auth, all commands, error cases,
byte-exact PUT/GET, UDP monitoring, 6 simultaneous controllers, abrupt disconnect).

## Design summary
* **Concurrency:** one detached pthread per TCP connection (simple, each session isolated, blocking I/O).
* **Framing:** per-session buffer; handles partial lines and several lines per `recv()`. PUT/GET move exactly `<filesize>` bytes (bytes already in the buffer after the command line are consumed first).
* **Errors:** `ERR 001 AUTH_FAILED`, `002 COMMAND_NOT_ALLOWED`, `003 NOT_AUTHENTICATED`, `004 FILE_TOO_LARGE`, `005 FILE_NOT_FOUND`, `006 UNKNOWN_COMMAND`, `007 BAD_REQUEST`, `008 BAD_FILENAME`, `009 MONITOR_ALREADY_RUNNING`, `010 MONITOR_NOT_RUNNING`, `011 STORAGE_ERROR`.
* **UDP monitoring:** one thread per session, `SYSINFO <cpu> <mem_mb> <uptime> SID:@@SID@@` every 2 s, stopped on `MONITOR STOP`, `QUIT` or disconnect.
* **Optional extension:** transfer throughput (bytes/s) reported by the Controller for PUT and GET.
* **Limits:** max upload 10 MB; filenames restricted to `[A-Za-z0-9._-]` (prevents path traversal); 3 failed AUTHs close the connection.
